Quiz02_01: 50 points
(FnA1szLongestMonoSubsequence)
Please state the status of this question:
1. Complete
2. Solved with testing? Yes, testing is included.
3. Solved without testing?
If solved, please BRIEFLY explain your strategy.
  
The algorithm runs in O(n^2).
1. DP Array Construction: 
    - Outer loop iteratets from i = n-2 down to 
    0 -> O(n) iterations
    - Inner loop iterates from j = i+1 to n-1 -> O(n)
    iterations in worst case
    - Total: O(n) x O(n) = O(n^2)
2. Finding maximum length (O(n)):
    - Single pass through dp array
3. Reconstruction (O(n^2)):
    - We need to find at most n indices (the subsequence length)
    - For each index, we scan forward through at most
    n elements
    - Total: O(n) x O(n) = O(n^2)

Algorithm expansion: 
- dp[i] stores the length of the longest ascending subsequence
starting at index i 
- We fill this array right-to-left: for each i, we check
all j > i where xs[j] >= xs[i], and set dp[i]=max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)
- to get the leftmost subsequence, we find the smallest starting
index with maximum length, then pick the leftmost valid next index
at each step

