Quiz02_02: 50 points
(sort1000WithNoRecursion)
Please state the status of this question:
1. Complete
2. Solved with testing? Yes, testing is included.
3. Solved without testing?
If solved, please BRIEFLY explain your strategy.

How the algorithm works:
- starts by treating each element as a sorted sub array 
of size 1
- merges adjacent pairs into sorted subarrays of size 2
- merges adjacent pairs into sorted subarrays of size 4
- continue doubling until the entire array is sorted

Time complexity: 
- outer loop runs log2(n) times (size doubles each iteration_)
- inner loop + merge processes all n elements each iteration
- total: O(n log n)

- algorithm only uses for loops and while loops, no recursive function calls

